### Tested versions

- Reproducible in: 4.7.2.stable [ed1daf0bf], 4.4.stable [4c311cbee], 4.8.dev (master) [e2b424692]. All three bake a byte-identical lightmap for the MRP below.
- Not reproducible with PR #123715 applied, on master (PR head [dece54b86]) and on 4.7.2.stable. Both bakes are byte-identical.

The dilation change comes from 054340bb6 (#100765), which is included in 4.4.stable and not in 4.3.stable.

### System information

Debian GNU/Linux 12 (bookworm), Linux 6.1, X11 - Godot v4.7.2.stable.official [ed1daf0bf] - Vulkan 1.3.230 (Forward+) - integrated Intel UHD Graphics 730 (Intel(R) Graphics (RKL GT1), Mesa 22.3.6) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-11400 @ 2.60GHz (12 threads)

### Issue description

The dilation pass of the lightmapper (`MODE_DILATE` in `modules/lightmapper_rd/lm_compute.glsl`) is meant to fill the empty texels around lightmap charts from a valid neighbor. Since 054340bb6 it also overwrites texels that already contain valid baked lighting:

```glsl
vec4 texel_color = texelFetch(sampler2DArray(source_light, linear_sampler), ivec3(atlas_pos, params.atlas_slice), 0);

for (int radius = 1; radius <= max_radius; radius++) {
	for (uint i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
		const ivec2 sample_pos = atlas_pos + directions[i] * radius;
		// (bounds check)
		vec4 neighbor_color = texelFetch(sampler2DArray(source_light, linear_sampler), ivec3(sample_pos, params.atlas_slice), 0);
		if (neighbor_color.a > 0.5) {
			texel_color = neighbor_color;
			break;
		}
	}

	if (texel_color.a > 0.5) {
		break;
	}
}
```

`texel_color` starts with the current texel, but the neighbor search runs even when that texel is already valid, and the first valid neighbor replaces it. Because the first direction searched is (-1, 0), many valid texels in this repro receive the value of the texel on their left in the atlas, producing an approximately one-texel shift along U.

In the MRP, a beam casts one straight shadow line across two identical floor tiles. The second tile is rotated 90 degrees, so its lightmap U axis runs along the line instead of across it. The one-texel shift then moves the line sideways on one tile only, and the line breaks where the tiles meet:

![Comparison](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/samjanny/godot-lightmap-dilation-mrp/22f8d509ef64e59b25344ae311f04c5186e8cdaf/docs/comparison.png)

Left: 4.7.2.stable. Right: the same project baked with PR #123715. Same scene, camera and bake settings.

Measured on the baked EXR (darkness weighted center of the line across the tiles, in texels), the line on the first tile is offset from the line on the second tile by +0.978 texels in 4.7.2.stable and by -0.005 texels with PR #123715. Comparing the two bakes texel by texel, every texel of the tiles that differs holds, in 4.7.2.stable, the value that the fixed build baked for one of its neighbors, in the order the dilation pass searches them (left: 126 texels, below: 10, right: 1). The empty texels around the charts, which dilation fills, are filled in both bakes with identical values.

**Expected behavior:** texels that already contain valid baked lighting keep their value, and dilation only fills empty texels. The shadow line is straight across both tiles.

**Actual behavior:** valid texels are replaced by a neighboring valid texel. The shadow line is displaced by about one texel where the tiles meet.

A fix is proposed in #123715: the neighbor search only runs while the current texel is empty, so valid texels keep their own value and empty texels are still filled.

Supporting evidence, not needed to reproduce the MRP: with a separately instrumented build on a larger scene, 57 of 57 traced valid texels were overwritten during dilation without the fix, and 0 of 57 with it (same RGBA before and after dilation). The 2 traced empty texels were filled in both builds, with the same values. Everything computed before dilation (raster position, normals, unocclude result, direct and accumulated light, ray hits) was identical between the two builds.

### Steps to reproduce

1. Clone or download https://github.com/samjanny/godot-lightmap-dilation-mrp and open it in Godot 4.7.2.stable.
2. Open `main.tscn`, select the `LightmapGI` node and click **Bake Lightmaps** in the 3D viewport toolbar. Save the lightmap data as `main.lmbake` when asked.
3. Save the scene (Ctrl+S) and run the project (F5). The bake does not mark the scene as modified, so without saving, F5 runs the scene without the lightmap.
4. The camera looks straight down at the two tiles: the shadow line breaks by one texel where they meet.

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

https://github.com/samjanny/godot-lightmap-dilation-mrp

Two PlaneMesh tiles (Add UV2, default texel size), a floating box, a static DirectionalLight3D and a LightmapGI with the denoiser off and the environment disabled. No scripts and no custom project settings. It reproduces on official builds and needs no custom engine build, shader instrumentation or test harness. The denoiser is only disabled to keep the baked values clean: with the default denoiser the break is the same (+0.988 texels, -0.005 with the fix). The README has the measurement details.
